$DIR/main.p:10:7: r holds a shared[Node], whose count is not atomic, and two tasks use it; use synced[T] (spec section 19.3)
    The package variable r is not sendable: it holds a shared[Node], whose count
    changes with plain arithmetic whenever a reference is copied out of it or
    dropped. Here the task started by task reader at main.p:17 uses it at
    main.p:10 in reader, and the task started by task reader at main.p:18 at
    main.p:10 in reader uses it too, so both may change the count at once.
    Go's garbage collector makes every pointer safe to share. Plutonium counts
    shared references without atomic instructions, which is only correct on one
    task.
    Use a synced[T] instead of the shared[T]: its count is atomic, so several
    tasks may hold references.
    (see "Sendable types" in the Plutonium spec, section 8.8)
    (run "pluto explain E2010" for a longer explanation)
